          text: 'The most general way to make an unsymmetrical ether, the [[ochem-williamson-ether-synthesis|Williamson ether synthesis]], is to let an **alkoxide** displace a halide or tosylate: $\\ce{RO- + R\'-X -> R-O-R\' + X-}$. Make the alkoxide with NaH (previous lesson), then add the alkyl halide. Every ether has two C–O bonds, so there are always **two** possible Williamson disconnections. Choose the one where the SN2 step has a methyl or primary electrophile.',
